leds: lgm-sso: default to falling-edge data clock to match vendor

The vendor's split sso-gpio driver defaults RZFL=1 (falling-edge data
clock) and only switches to rising-edge when intel,sso-rising is set
in the DT. Mainline hard-codes DATA_CLK_EDGE=0 (rising) so on boards
whose external shift register is wired for the vendor default, the
data clocked out doesn't latch and writes to SSO_CPU never appear at
the LED outputs.

Match the vendor default by setting DATA_CLK_EDGE=1.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
--- a/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@
 #define MAX_FREQ_RANK			10
 #define DEF_GPTC_CLK_RATE		200000000
 #define SSO_DEF_BRIGHTNESS		LED_HALF
-#define DATA_CLK_EDGE			0 /* 0-rising, 1-falling */
+#define DATA_CLK_EDGE			1 /* 0-rising, 1-falling */
 
 static const u32 freq_div_tbl[] = {4000, 2000, 1000, 800};
 static const int freq_tbl[] = {2, 4, 8, 10, 50000, 100000, 200000, 250000};
